index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Cliques","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/reductions(_:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/reductions(_:)","title":"reductions(_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reductions"},{"kind":"text","text":"(("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier"